{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-010e7cdb5699e4339523","statement":"If $n=3$ and $X = \\{\\varepsilon_1-\\varepsilon_2\\}$, then $\\fh^X = \\C h^1$, where $h^1 = H_1 + H_2 -2 H_3$. In particular, $\\det D_\\delta^X = 2(H_1 + H_2 - 2 H_3)^2$. If $X = \\emptyset$ and $n\\geq 3$, then $\\fh^X = \\fh$, and $\\det D_\\delta^X = 2^{n-1}H_1\\cdots H_n(\\frac{1}{H_1}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{H_n})$ (see <<cite:GS08>>).","source_id":"arXiv:1902.03512","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"e528a7a4b142734ee3a16a8e5931f883ec164c526312104ff95b794ca00e0a5a","kind":"example","label":"Example 3","ref_key":"","name":"","order":3,"deps":[],"cite_keys":["GS08"],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.03512","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"e85edb0921f1b034cf532737743ad6ef03c3c82b74116f1220f34efc30999f1b","line":560,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:18:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":321,"math_hints":50}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1902.03512","title":"Non-standard Verma type modules for $\\fq(n)^{(2)}$","abstract":"We study non-standard Verma type modules over the Kac-Moody queer Lie superalgebra $\\mathfrak{q}(n)^{(2)}$. We give a sufficient condition under which such modules are irreducible. We also give a classification of all irreducible diagonal $\\mathbb{Z}$-graded modules over certain Heisenberg Lie superalgebras contained in $\\mathfrak{q}(n)^{(2)}$.","authors":["Lucas Calixto","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2019","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.03512","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"C":"\\mathbb{C}","Z":"\\mathbb{Z}","N":"\\mathbb{N}","ch":"\\mathrm{ch}","g":"\\mathfrak{g}","fm":"\\mathfrak{m}","fq":"\\mathfrak{q}","fh":"\\mathfrak{h}","fn":"\\mathfrak{n}","fa":"\\mathfrak{a}","fsl":"\\mathfrak{sl}","fgl":"\\mathfrak{gl}","fu":"\\mathfrak{u}","fk":"\\mathf